/*
 * EGL's and OpenGL ES's entry points as guest code calls them, each an adapter to ANGLE's function of the same name as
 * Windows' convention has it (MG_GLAPI): x86_64 and x86 on desktop Windows (mg_gl_adapters.c, docs/DESKTOP.md).
 * GENERATED by tools/gl-adapters.py from Khronos' headers as the NDK ships them -- do not edit; run it again.
 *
 * h_<name> is ANGLE's function (a slot mg_gl_adapter fills), a_<name> the adapter. Every handle and pointer is a pointer
 * here, every other type the C type of its width: what a calling convention looks at.
 */
/*
 * Declared in: EGL/egl.h (44), EGL/eglext.h (100), EGL/eglext_angle.h (8), GLES3/gl32.h (358), GLES3/gl31.h (314), GLES3/gl3.h (246), GLES2/gl2.h (142), GLES2/gl2ext.h (494), GLES/gl.h (145), GLES/glext.h (150).
 * Written by hand in mg_gl_adapters.c:
 *   eglDebugMessageControlKHR, which takes an EGLDEBUGPROCKHR
 *   eglQueryDebugKHR, which gives back the EGLDEBUGPROCKHR it was given (EGL_DEBUG_CALLBACK_KHR)
 *   eglSetBlobCacheFuncsANDROID, which takes an EGLSetBlobFuncANDROID and an EGLGetBlobFuncANDROID
 *   glDebugMessageCallback, which takes a GLDEBUGPROC
 *   glDebugMessageCallbackKHR, which takes a GLDEBUGPROCKHR
 *   glGetPointerv, which gives back the GLDEBUGPROC it was given (GL_DEBUG_CALLBACK_FUNCTION)
 *   glGetPointervKHR, which gives back the GLDEBUGPROCKHR it was given (GL_DEBUG_CALLBACK_FUNCTION).
 * Left out, with no adapter (asked for, "no such function"):
 *   eglGetProcAddress: the core answers it itself (mg_egl_resolve), with adapters
 *   glGetVkProcAddrNV: gives a function of the driver's (GL_NV_draw_vulkan_image, which ANGLE has not).
 */

